          "quote": "Subject to the other terms of this Section 9.3, during the Royalty Term, Sanofi shall make quarterly royalty payments to RevMed on aggregate Net Sales of each Product sold outside the United States during a Calendar Year at the applicable royalty rates as set forth below.",
          "rationale": "The Agreement imposes no minimum purchase, volume or take-or-pay commitment on Sanofi, so it sits at the preferred position. Sanofi's payment obligations are event- or usage-based only: a one-time upfront payment (§9.1), milestone payments triggered only on first achievement of a Milestone Event and capped in aggregate (§9.2), royalties on actual Net Sales during the Royalty Term (§9.3), and reimbursement of RevMed R&D Costs actually \"incurred by or on behalf of RevMed ... in the performance of its activities under the Research Plan\" per the approved Research Budget (§4.5(a)). There are no volume caps on Sanofi, no shortfall or penalty mechanic, and no committed minimum spend: the Research Budget is an estimate governed by the JSC/JRDC and, from CY2021 onward, subject to Sanofi's final decision-making power (§4.2(a)(ii)-(iii)). Manufacturing/supply is left to a future Supply Agreement to be negotiated (§7.3) with no requirements or minimum-order term, and the only purchase obligation on termination falls on RevMed (§12.5 inventory purchase), which benefits us. Sanofi also retains termination for convenience in its entirety or country/Product-by-Product (§12.2(a)(i)), providing a clean exit. No redline required.",
